# Flyleaf — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. .env* is gitignored; never commit a real
# key, and never put a secret in a VITE_ variable — everything prefixed VITE_
# is compiled into the JavaScript the browser downloads and is readable by
# anyone who opens the app.

# ---- Sync to the reader's own Google Drive (optional) ----

# The OAuth client ID from Google Cloud Console. PUBLIC BY DESIGN: a client ID
# is not a credential, it is compiled into every browser bundle, and Google
# documents it as such — which is why it is allowed a VITE_ prefix when nothing
# else secret is. Unset, the "Sync across devices" row does not exist and the
# app is local-only, which is its default state anyway.
#
# The matching client SECRET is never used by this app. The sign-in is Google
# Identity Services' token flow, which has no secret and no redirect URI. Do
# not copy the secret into this file, the repo, or anywhere else.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ---- Tip jar (optional; the whole app works without it) ----

# Set to 1 to show the "buy the maker a coffee" card in Settings. Leave it
# unset and the card does not exist. Setting this WITHOUT the secret below
# gives readers a card that opens onto an error, so set both or neither.
VITE_TIP_JAR=

# Paystack secret key — SERVER ONLY. Never prefixed VITE_, never imported from
# anything in src/, never pasted into the repo. It is read by api/tip.ts at
# request time and nowhere else.
#
# Local: put the TEST key (sk_test_...) in .env.local and run `vercel dev`.
# Production: add it in the Vercel dashboard under Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables (or `vercel env add PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY production`),
# using the LIVE key (sk_live_...) once Paystack has verified the account.
#
# Paystack's public key (pk_...) is not needed anywhere: the checkout is opened
# server-side, so the browser never talks to Paystack directly.
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional, server-only. Which currencies this Paystack account can settle,
# comma-separated — the tip jar offers each reader the one their country uses,
# but only from this list, because Paystack refuses a currency the account has
# not enabled. Unset means NGN only, which every Nigerian account has. Add
# more (e.g. NGN,USD) only after enabling them on the Paystack dashboard;
# the jar knows NGN, USD, GHS, ZAR and KES.
PAYSTACK_CURRENCIES=

# Optional, server-only. Where Paystack returns a supporter after checkout.
# Left unset, the function uses the deployment URL Vercel provides, and falls
# back to the request's own origin when running locally. Set it to your custom
# domain (https://example.com, no trailing slash) once you have one.
TIP_RETURN_ORIGIN=
